@{
    ViewData["Title"] = ".NET Core Overview";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "DotNetCore";
    ViewData["ActivePage"] = "DotNetCoreOverview";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <div class="mb-4">
        <p class="text-uppercase text-muted fw-semibold small">Modern .NET</p>
        <h1 class="mb-3">Why .NET Core matters</h1>
        <p class="lead">.NET Core (now part of the unified .NET) is the cross-platform runtime and SDK that powers high-performance web, cloud, desktop, and containerized applications. It is designed to be lean, fast, and easy to deploy anywhere.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="p-4 bg-white border rounded-4 shadow-sm h-100">
                <h2 class="h5">Key design goals</h2>
                <ul class="mb-0">
                    <li><strong>Performance-first:</strong> a highly optimized runtime with tiered JIT, ready-to-run (R2R), and hardware intrinsics.</li>
                    <li><strong>Cross-platform parity:</strong> the same APIs and tooling on Windows, Linux, and macOS.</li>
                    <li><strong>Modular &amp; lightweight:</strong> applications ship only the packages they need, reducing deployment size.</li>
                    <li><strong>Cloud native:</strong> first-class support for containers, microservices, and DevOps workflows.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="p-4 bg-white border rounded-4 shadow-sm h-100">
                <h2 class="h5">What you build with it</h2>
                <ul class="mb-0">
                    <li>HTTP APIs and real-time apps with ASP.NET Core.</li>
                    <li>Background workers, message processors, and event-driven services.</li>
                    <li>Cross-platform CLI tools for automation and developer productivity.</li>
                    <li>Microservices packaged as containers for Kubernetes or Azure Container Apps.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5 p-4 bg-light border rounded-3">
        <h2 class="h5">Deployment snapshot</h2>
        <p class="mb-2">A typical deployment flow for a production-ready API:</p>
        <ol class="mb-0">
            <li>Develop locally with the .NET SDK and minimal APIs or controllers.</li>
            <li>Containerize using a multi-stage Dockerfile to keep the final image slim.</li>
            <li>Push to a registry (Azure Container Registry, Docker Hub) and promote via CI/CD.</li>
            <li>Run on orchestrators such as AKS, Kubernetes, or Azure App Service with autoscale rules.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>
